WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.640
Speaker 1: All right, let's start today with
a covid update, we haven't done this for a

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.820
while, and increasingly the numbers in the
United States are looking better and better

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.530
as vaccination takes place.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.790
We've seen the slowdown due to vaccine hesitancy.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.170
We will talk about it.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:19.820
We have also now seen evidence that the vaccines
work well enough against all major variants.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.580
We will talk about that momentarily.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:29.500
But first of all, cases, cases which peaked
at more than two hundred and fifty five thousand

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:36.219
cases per day in mid-January, an outrageous
number, not illegal, but certainly an immoral

00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:37.219
number.

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:42.429
As I like to say, cases are now down under
50000 thousand cases per day for the first

00:00:42.429 --> 00:00:44.200
time since October of twenty twenty.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:50.969
It's been seven months since cases have been
this low, down to about 47000 per day as of

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:52.269
yesterday.

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:57.339
This is now down more than 80 percent from
the peak in mid-January.

00:00:57.339 --> 00:01:02.730
And these numbers should continue down and
look even better by Memorial Day, certainly

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:03.730
by mid-June.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:11.469
As far as deaths go, deaths peaked in late
January at nearly thirty five hundred deaths

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:16.159
per day, more than a 9/11 every single day.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:21.670
And those are now also down more than 80 percent
to about six seventy five a day.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:24.369
Still horrible, but dramatically lower.

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:31.070
And understand that daily deaths in the US
have not been below 700 a day since July of

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.270
last summer.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.299
So that is going very much in the right direction.

00:01:34.299 --> 00:01:37.719
Deaths as low as they've been in basically
10 months now.

00:01:37.719 --> 00:01:42.979
Globally, cases were coming down and are coming
down in the US globally.

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:49.189
We did see a spike led by countries like India
and Brazil, among others, that has also turned

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:51.539
around not by much, but globally.

00:01:51.539 --> 00:01:55.750
Cases are now down about three to four percent
from the peak that happened about 10 days

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.750
ago.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:02.969
We hope that the global numbers will also
start coming down more significantly as vaccines

00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:04.750
get to more and more countries.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:11.140
And we will speak momentarily about Joe Biden
coming out in support of lifting or not enforcing

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.690
patents on vaccines.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.730
I actually don't think that's going to make
a difference, but I'm going to tell you why

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.430
in the next segment.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:23.770
Earlier this week, I did tell you that vaccination
is a growing problem in the sense that supply

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.720
is now exceeding demand in many places.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:32.790
And we've seen average daily doses decline
from their high of about three point four

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:37.870
million a day now down to just two point one
million doses per day over the last week.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:42.970
That's not good, but it will still get us
where we need to go as long as it continues.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:48.160
But the decline in doses led Joe Biden to
announce a new vaccination initiative earlier

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.160
this week.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.480
We talked about it yesterday.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.260
CVS Pharmacy has already met the call.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:59.050
They are going to be offering walk in vaccination,
no appointment necessary at thousands of pharmacies

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.740
across the country.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:06.310
But the really good news about vaccines is
they work on the variance of concern.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:12.140
Dr. Eric Topol, former guest on the show,
published yesterday, a great infographics

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.790
showing us that of all of the relevant variants
so far, there's the British, South African

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:17.940
and Brazilian.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.460
Then there's the New York, California and
India variants.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:26.511
We have at least some evidence that the vaccines
work, for example, with the UK, South Africa

00:03:26.511 --> 00:03:28.050
and Brazil variants.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:33.760
We now have lab studies, randomized clinical
trials and real world evidence that the vaccines

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.560
work well enough on those variants, that if
we keep vaccinating, we can get out of this

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.400
for the New York, California and India variants.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.871
We don't yet have the randomized controlled
trials, but we have lab studies and we have

00:03:46.871 --> 00:03:47.990
real world evidence.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.490
So we have a path out of this.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:55.360
Moderna and Fizer at minimum, are working
on Booster's that will be tweaked for the

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.140
variance for the fall or winter.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.760
So the path is clear by Memorial Day.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.640
We will have a better situation than we have
today and a little deeper, you know, early

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:10.810
summer, it will be even better if people keep
getting vaccinated.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:05:14.850
Let's talk next about 

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:20.670
the patents.

